            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I think user defined types make sense.\nIf one is dabbling with Cython types, then it is explicit effort.\nAnd if one has bothered to write a cython class, then return types are part of the point and this is what is desirable anyways.\n\nHowever, I think ideally Pure Python code would compile safely when no explicit typing effort was made.\n\n---\n\nNow that I know about `len` it seems like a very useful thing to have - it is not uncommon that `len` becomes one of bottlenecks in tight loops of Python. However, I would suggest that it might be better to have it other way round - opt in.\n```python\nn: cython.Py_ssize_t = len(c)\n```",
